{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress (max_addr 0x00000000, tohost FAIL 0xdead) instead of sequential NOP fetches. mem_do_wdata is driven to 1 on !resetn || mem_done where 0 is expected, falsely holding a write request after every transaction. Root cause is line 1953 `mem_do_wdata <= 1` in the clear block, blocking the rinst fetch path from re-arming.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1949,7 +1949,7 @@
 		if (!resetn || mem_done) begin
 			mem_do_prefetch <= 0;
 			mem_do_rinst <= 0;
 			mem_do_rdata <= 0;
-			mem_do_wdata <= 1;
+			mem_do_wdata <= 0;
 		end", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead) with forward progress max_addr > 0x00000000"}

